% ============================================================================
% farm-animal-maintenance-level.query — a worked recall over the
% agriculture farm-animal-maintenance-level library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how much care does a
% sheep need?": it states no agriculture fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `farm_animal_maintenance_level` rows and
% returns the level + the table's source/locator/trust. An animal the
% cited spans give no maintenance level for abstains honestly — the
% engine never invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli farm-animal-maintenance-level.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "farm-animal-maintenance-level.adj"

? farm_animal_maintenance_level(sheep, $Level)               % expect low_maintenance
? farm_animal_maintenance_level($Animal, low_maintenance)    % reverse bind — expect sheep
? farm_animal_maintenance_level(goat, $Level)                 % expect abstain — goat's own cited span states no husbandry-difficulty descriptor
